# counter harness. One force call is one RgpotCounter.calculate entry.
# GeometryOptimization LBFGS, CG, and GradientDescent call the spec potential.
# The callback stops at the problem Euclidean force norm, or the noise-aware rule.
# v2 success is under the cap, at that stop, and Hessian index 0.
# GeometryOptimization 0.1.6 OptimLBFGS uses the Hager-Zhang initial step. BackTracking linesearch of order 2 and maxstep 0.8 bohr. The iteration ceiling is the force-call cap. The potential is the harness callback. The callback stops at the Euclidean force norm 0.001 eV/Å. Positions are angstrom and the energy is eV. The solver converts those to atomic units internally. The recorded force is the spec gradient in eV/Å.
